# .trivyignore file - Place this in your repository root
# This file allows you to ignore specific CVEs that are not applicable to your application

# Common false positives or non-applicable vulnerabilities for Java applications

# Log4j vulnerabilities (if you're not using log4j or using a safe version)
# CVE-2021-44228
# CVE-2021-45046
# CVE-2021-45105
# CVE-2021-44832

# Spring Framework vulnerabilities (if using a safe version)
# CVE-2022-22965
# CVE-2022-22950

# JVM/OpenJDK vulnerabilities that are not exploitable in container environments
# CVE-2023-21930
# CVE-2023-21967
# CVE-2023-21968

# Will be fixed by updating Spring Boot in ticket [JIRA-123].
CVE-2025-24813 # Critical vulnerability in tomcat-embed-core
CVE-2024-38821 # Critical vulnerability in spring-security-web
CVE-2024-1597  # Critical vulnerability in leave-service (postgresql-driver)

# OS-level vulnerabilities that don't affect the application
# Uncomment these if they're causing issues and you've verified they don't affect your app
# CVE-2022-3219
# CVE-2022-3996
# CVE-2023-0464

# Example: Ignore specific vulnerability in a specific package
# CVE-2023-1234 in package-name

